insert into bible_entries (entry_date, ot_passage, ot_notes, nt_passage, nt_notes) values
  ('2023-10-12', $b$Isaiah 39:1-40:31$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Hezekiah was flexing on his neighbors, I guess that's kinda sinful because God then says that he’s gonna be looted of all his possessions one day, but then Hezekiah says, “thats chill” because he assumes its not going to be in his lifespan which is kinda bogus I felt like</p></li><li><p>People are like grass (RIP)</p></li><li><p>Nations are like drops in buckets</p></li><li><p>Always wanted to see lebanon in real life</p></li><li><p>Soar on wings like eagles, run will not grow faint….</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$Colossians 4$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Devote yourselves to prayer!</p></li><li><p>Apparently there's a different guy named “Jesus, who is called Justus” in verse 11. Never realized.</p></li></ul>$b$),
  ('2023-10-13', $b$Isaiah 41:1-42:25$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>The LORD GOD is pretty mighty.</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$1 Thessalonians 1$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Another Paul letter writing to the Thessalonians dudes. Pretty short.</p></li></ul>$b$),
  ('2023-10-14', $b$Isaiah 43:1-44:28$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>God is the first and the last</p></li><li><p>There is no other God other than God…nice.</p></li><li><p>Verses 13-20 always made idols sound even stupider than they already were. People back then were kinda dumb I guess. (people nowadays also are too ofc)</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$1 Thessalonians 2$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Paul was treated outrageously in Philippi! No surprise there.</p></li><li><p>Paul longs to see the thessalonians.</p></li></ul>$b$),
  ('2023-10-15', $b$Isaiah 45:1-46:13$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>He forms the light and creates the darkness? NIV is weird</p></li><li><p>Ok switched it to standard edition? Where is esv online :\</p></li><li><p>Every knee shall bow every tongue confess</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$1 Thessalonians 3$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Paul thought it was best to be left by athens. OK.</p></li></ul>$b$),
  ('2023-10-16', $b$Isaiah 47:1-49:26$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>I wonder what the virgin daughter of Babylon refers to.</p></li><li><p>Same goes for daughter of Chaldeans</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$1 Thessalonians 4:1-18$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>It is God’s will to avoid sexual immorality 😬, control our own bodies 😬</p></li><li><p>Mind your own affairs, work with your own hands</p></li></ul>$b$),
  ('2023-10-17', $b$Isaiah 50-52$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>God is kinda sarcastic sometimes</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$1 Thessalonians 5$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>We belong to the day, so let’s be sober….?</p></li><li><p>Encourage our brothers and build one another up</p></li></ul>$b$),
  ('2023-10-18', $b$Isaiah 53:1-55:13$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Surely he took up our pain and bore our suffering</p></li><li><p>Pierced for our transgressions, crushed for our iniquities</p></li><li><p>We all like sheep have gone astray</p></li><li><p>Seek the LORD while he may be found; call on him when he is near</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$2 Thessalonians 1$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Those who do not know God will suffer the punishment of eternal damnation!!!</p></li></ul>$b$),
  ('2023-10-19', $b$Isaiah 56:1-58:14$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Maintain justice and do what is right</p></li><li><p>There is no peace for the wicked</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$2 Thessalonians 2:1-17$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Don't be fooled by those who say that Jesus is coming today or the end of the world is tomorrow. They don't know.</p></li></ul>$b$),
  ('2023-10-20', $b$Isaiah 59:1-61:11$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Oops</p></li></ul>$b$, null, null),
  ('2023-10-21', $b$Isaiah 62:1-64:12$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>We are the clay, you are the potter</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$1 Timothy 1$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>The law is not made for the righteous but for the wicked, etc.</p></li></ul>$b$),
  ('2023-10-22', $b$Isaiah 65:1-66:24$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>See, i will create a new heaven and earth, the former things will not be remembered</p></li><li><p>The wolf and the lamb will feed together</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$1 Timothy 2:1-15$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>I want the women to dress modestly</p></li><li><p>Submissive women 😳</p></li></ul>$b$),
  ('2023-10-23', $b$Jeremiah 1:1-2:37$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Israel disobeying God again</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$1 Timothy 3:1-16$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Whoever aspires to be an “overseer” (NIV is wack) must be faithful to his wife, temperate, self controlled, respectable, etc.</p></li></ul>$b$),
  ('2023-10-24', $b$Jeremiah 3:1-5:31$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>If a man divorces his wife, and she leaves and marries another man, should he return to her again? Would not the land be completely defiled?</p></li><li><p>Don't be a prostitute, bro.</p></li><li><p>Somehow God allows israel to come back to him even after all that prostitutin’ (and me too)</p></li><li><p>We are all well fed, lusty stallions, each one craving for his neighbor’s wife. Should we not be punished for this?</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$1 Timothy 4$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Some will abandon the faith and follow demons and lies (hopefully not me)</p></li><li><p>Forbidding marriage and abstaining from certain foods is foolish, God made everything to be enjoyed (in the right way)</p></li><li><p>Everything God created is good</p></li><li><p>Physical training is of some value but godliness has value for all things</p></li><li><p>Don't let anyone look down on you because you are young</p></li></ul>$b$),
  ('2023-10-25', $b$Jeremiah 6:1-8-22$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Flee for safety, people of benjamin!</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$1 Timothy 5:1-25$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Do not rebuke an older man harshly, but treat him like a father</p></li><li><p>Treat younger men as brothers</p></li><li><p>The sins of some are obvious</p></li><li><p>In the same way, the good deeds of some are obvious too…?</p></li></ul>$b$),
  ('2023-10-26', $b$Jeremiah 9:1-11:23$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Let not the wise boast of their wisdom, or the strong boast of their strength, or the rich boast of their riches.</p></li><li><p>Do not be “circumcised” only in the flesh</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$1 Timothy 6$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Show your masters respect</p></li><li><p>Godliness with contentment is great gain</p></li><li><p>We brought nothing into this world, we can take nothing out</p></li><li><p>The love of money is the root of all kinds of evil</p></li><li><p>Fight the good fight</p></li><li><p>Don't put your hope in your wealth</p></li><li><p>Put yo hope in God</p></li></ul>$b$),
  ('2023-10-27', $b$Jeremiah 12:1-14:22$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>You are righteous, lord</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$2 Timothy 1$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>The spirit of God does not make us timid, but in fact gives us power, love, and self discipline.</p></li></ul>$b$),
  ('2023-10-28', $b$Jeremiah 15:1-17:27$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Dang, at this point in time God was so mad at israel that he said even if moses and samuel stood in front of him he’d still say nah</p></li><li><p>Can a man break iron-iron from the north-or bronze? I don't know, the rhetorical answer is probably no but i've seen youtube videos of people doing it 😳</p></li><li><p>If you repent, he will restore you</p></li><li><p>God is really cracking down on them here</p></li><li><p>Cursed is the one who trusts in man, who draws strength from mere flesh, who turns away from the Lord.</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$2 Timothy 2:1-26$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Anyone who competes as an athlete does not recieve the victor’s crown unless abiding by the rules</p></li><li><p>If we died with him, we will also live with him</p></li><li><p>If we disown him, he will disown us</p></li><li><p>Flee the evil desires of youth</p></li><li><p>Opponents must be gently instructed</p></li></ul>$b$),
  ('2023-10-29', $b$Jeremiah 18:1-19:15$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>More on God talking about Israel's disobedience.</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$2 Timothy 3$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>There will be terrible times in the last days.</p></li><li><p>There will be lovers of themselves, of money, boastful, proud, disobedient to their parents, etc.</p></li><li><p>Anyone who wants to live a godly life will be persecuted.</p></li><li><p>All scripture is God breathed and useful for teaching, rebuking, correcting and training in righteousness.</p></li></ul>$b$),
  ('2023-10-30', $b$Jeremiah 20:1-21:14$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Pashhur’s name got changed from Pashhur to Terror on Every Side. Ok.</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$2 Timothy 4$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Preach the word</p></li><li><p>Keep your head in all situations</p></li><li><p>Fight the good fight, finish the race, keep the faith</p></li><li><p>Rip Demas, whoever that guy was</p></li><li><p>Alexander the metalworker better watch out 😳</p></li><li><p>Pretty sure Paul dies somewhen around here.</p></li></ul>$b$),
  ('2023-10-31', $b$Jeremiah 22:1-23:40$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Rescue from the hand of the oppressor the one that has been robbed</p></li><li><p>Do no wrong or violence to the foreigner</p></li><li><p>Do I not fill the heaven and the earth? Declares the LORD</p></li><li><p>Is not my word like fire, or a hammer that breaks a rock to pieces?</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$Titus 1$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Don't claim to know God, but let your actions deny him.</p></li></ul>$b$),
  ('2023-11-01', $b$Jeremiah 24:1-26:24$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>When is God going to stop saying he’s going to utterly demolish israel…giving them a lot of time to repent, wow</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$Titus 2:1-15$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Encourage the young men to be SELF CONTROLLED</p></li><li><p>Do not let anyone despise you</p></li><li><p>Encourage and rebuke with all authority</p></li></ul>$b$),
  ('2023-11-02', $b$Jeremiah 27:1-29:32$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Yoke</p></li><li><p>Rip hananiah. Why’d he lie in the first place?</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$Titus 3:1-15$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Don't slander</p></li><li><p>Be subject to rulers and authorities</p></li><li><p>Be peaceable and considerate</p></li><li><p>He saved us, not because of anything we have done but instead, through his mercy</p></li><li><p>Warn a person once, then a second time. After that, have nothing to do with them. I think this definitely isn't meant to be taken literally, though.</p></li></ul>$b$),
  ('2023-11-03', $b$Jeremiah 30:1-31:40$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Can a man bear children? No…</p></li><li><p>God will surely save you! Yay!</p></li><li><p>He will refresh the weary and satisfy the faint</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$Our daily bread is tripping today.$b$, null),
  ('2023-11-04', $b$Jeremiah 32:1-33:26$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Nothing is too hard for you</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$Hebrews 1:1-14$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>The son is the radiance of God’s glory and the exact representation of God’s being</p></li><li><p>You laid the foundation of the earth, and the heavens are the work of your hands</p></li></ul>$b$),
  ('2023-11-05', $b$Jeremiah 34:1-36:32$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Scrolls. Okay.</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$Hebrews 2:1-18$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>We must pay most careful attention to what we have heard</p></li><li><p>What is mankind that you are so mindful of? Thanks, God. For being mindful of me. I hope so. I know. Kinda.</p></li><li><p>So that by the grace of God he might taste death for everyone</p></li><li><p>I will put my trust in him</p></li></ul>$b$),
  ('2023-11-06', $b$Jeremiah 37:1-39:18$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Nobody is paying attention to God’s word. Tragic.</p></li><li><p>Pharaoh's army said, nah</p></li><li><p>Ebed malek, nice job.</p></li><li><p>The fall of jerusalem. Finally,</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$Hebrews 3:1-19$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>God is the builder of everything</p></li><li><p>Do not harden your hearts!!!</p></li><li><p>Encourage one another daily</p></li></ul>$b$),
  ('2023-11-07', $b$Jeremiah 40:1-42:22$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>That's kinda sad. Gedaliaih trusted that Ishmeal wouldnt kill him and then Ishmeal killed him.</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$Hebrews 4:1-16$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Today, if you hear his voice, do not harden your hearts.</p></li><li><p>Let us then approach God’s throne of grace with confidence, that we may recieve mercy and find grace to help us in our times of need.</p></li></ul>$b$),
  ('2023-11-08', $b$Jeremiah 43:1-45:5$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>I hope I'm not like Israel, disobeying God’s blatant commands day by day, forgiveness after forgiveness. I hope so.</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$Hebrews 5$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>The “high priest” is subject to weakness, just like the rest of us. So in today’s day, this probably means pastors.</p></li></ul>$b$),
  ('2023-11-09', $b$Jeremiah 46:1-47:7$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>L for egypt</p></li><li><p>“Though I completely destroy all the nations among which I scatter you, I will not <em>completely</em> destroy you”. Wow, pretty generous, God.</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$Hebrews 6$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Let us move beyond the elementary teachings about christ and be taken forward in maturity</p></li><li><p>Land that produces thorns and thistles is worthless. In the end it will be burned.</p></li><li><p>God is not unjust, he will not forget your work and the love that you have shown him.</p></li></ul>$b$),
  ('2023-11-10', $b$Jeremiah 48:1-49:39$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Concerning MOAB…concerning mother of all balloons from btd6?!?!</p></li><li><p>Woe to nebo, huh. Woe to me.</p></li><li><p>Since you trust in your deeds and riches, you too will be captured…don't be like that guy.</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$Hebrews 7:1-28$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Melchizedek means “king of righteousness”</p></li></ul>$b$),
  ('2023-11-11', $b$Jeremiah 50:1-46$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Looks like it's an L for Babylon this time.</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$Hebrews 8:1-13$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Priests</p></li></ul>$b$),
  ('2023-11-12', $b$Jeremiah 51:1-52:34$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Babylon L…still?</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$Hebrews 9:1-28$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>The blood of Christ will cleanse us</p></li><li><p>He has appeared once and for all for the culmination of the ages to do away with sin, yata!</p></li><li><p>He will appear a second time to bring salvation to those who are waiting for him</p></li></ul>$b$),
  ('2023-11-13', $b$Lamentations 1-2$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Fitting to start lamentations with a lament. I've been reading too many laments.</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$Hebrews 10:1-18$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>I will put my law in their hearts, and I will write them in their minds.</p></li><li><p>Their sins and lawless acts i will remember no more</p></li><li><p>And where these have been forgiven, sacrifice for sin is no longer necessary</p></li></ul>$b$),
  ('2023-11-14', $b$Lamentations 3-5$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Because of the Lord’s great love we are not consumed</p></li><li><p>The Lord is good to those whose hope is in him</p></li><li><p>It is good to wait quietly for the salvation of the Lord</p></li><li><p>No one is cast off by the Lord forever</p></li><li><p>Let us examine our ways and test them</p></li><li><p>The part of about mothers cooking their own children is kinda sad and gross</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$Hebrews 10:19-39$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Let us hold unswervingly to the hope we profess</p></li><li><p>Spur one another toward love and good deeds</p></li></ul>$b$),
  ('2023-11-15', $b$Ezekiel 1:1-2:10$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Lapis lazuli hehehe</p></li><li><p>The glory of God is kinda spooky</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$Hebrews 11:1-19$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Faith is confidence in what we hope for and things unseen</p></li><li><p>By faith, by faith, by faith….</p></li></ul>$b$),
  ('2023-11-16', $b$Ezekiel 3:1-4:17$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Yummy scroll</p></li><li><p>“Rumbling”</p></li><li><p>Whoever will listen let them listen, whoever will refuse let them refuse</p></li><li><p>Verse 15 kinda weird…?</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$Hebrews 11:20-40$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Everybody does their things through faith. Through faith I must work out. Through faith I must do my skincare. Through faith I must violin, school, make it to Madison, everything. God give me faith!!!</p></li><li><p>God has planned something better for us</p></li></ul>$b$),
  ('2023-11-17', $b$Ezekiel 5:1-7:27$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Shaving with a sword?</p></li><li><p>Interesting choice of using his hair as a show of your power, God.</p></li><li><p>When God is against you, you have no hope.</p></li><li><p>“Then they will know that I am the Lord” 😱</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$Hebrews 12$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Sin so easily entangles.</p></li><li><p>Run with perseverance the race marked out for us, fixing our eyes upon jesus!</p></li><li><p>Do not lose heart when he disciplines you, the Lord disciplines everyone he loves</p></li><li><p>What children are not disciplined by their father?</p></li><li><p>Discipline will produce a harvest of righteousness and peace</p></li><li><p>Make an effort to live in peace with everyone</p></li><li><p>Our God is a consuming fire. 🔥</p></li></ul>$b$),
  ('2023-11-18', $b$Ezekiel 8:1-10:22$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Don't follow idols. God will get you.</p></li><li><p>God has executioners, apparently. Imagine God’s executioners walking down your town killing people. Spooky.</p></li><li><p>Spooky bible creatures. Cherubim.</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$Hebrews 13:1-25$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Don't forget to show hospitality to strangers, because they might be angels!</p></li><li><p>Marriage should be honored by all, marriage should be kept pure</p></li><li><p>Keep your lives free from the love of money and be content with what you have</p></li><li><p>God has said, I will never leave you, never will I forsake you</p></li></ul>$b$),
  ('2023-11-19', $b$Ezekiel 11:1-13:23$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Israel gotta step it up</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$James 1$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>The testing of your faith produces perseverance</p></li><li><p>Ask God for wisdom. Please?</p></li><li><p>Do not doubt when you ask, otherwise you're kinda like a wave of the sea…don't expect anything from the Lord.</p></li><li><p>Blessed is the one who perseveres through a trial</p></li><li><p>God tempts no one, each person is tempted by their own desire</p></li><li><p>Quick to listen, slow to speak, slow to anger</p></li><li><p>Don't merely listen to the word, do what it says.</p></li></ul>$b$),
  ('2023-11-20', $b$Ezekiel 14:1-15:8$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Don't idol! That made no grammatical sense.</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$James 2:1-26$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Mercy triumphs over judgment?</p></li><li><p>What good is faith without deeds? Hm, not very good.</p></li><li><p>As the body without spirit is dead, so faith without works is ded. Ded m&amp;m.</p></li></ul>$b$),
  ('2023-11-21', $b$Ezekiel 16:1-17:24$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>…your neighbors with large genitals?</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$James 3:1-18$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Just like how a small rudder steers a large ship, the tongue makes great boasts</p></li><li><p>Spark starts a wildfire, etc.</p></li><li><p>Peacemakers who sow in peace reap a harvest of righteousness.</p></li></ul><p>Control your tongue.</p>$b$),
  ('2023-11-27', $b$Ezekiel 30:1-32:32$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Rip pharoah’s arms.</p></li><li><p>Gory!!!</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$1 Peter 4:1-19$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Above all, love one another deeeppllyy</p></li><li><p>Use whatever gift you have to serve others</p></li><li><p>Hardships because of your faith in jesus is a blessing</p></li></ul><p>Use whatever gift you have to serve God.</p>$b$),
  ('2023-11-28', $b$Ezekiel 33:1-34:31$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Heed warnings</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$1 Peter 5:1-14$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>God opposes the proud but shows favor to the humble</p></li><li><p>The devil prowls around searching for someone to devour…don't let it be you!</p></li></ul><p>Be humble.</p>$b$),
  ('2023-11-29', $b$Ezekiel 35:1-36:38$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Seems like God is chill with the israelites again</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$2 Peter 1$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Make every effort to add to your faith, to your goodness, to your knowledge, to your self control, etc.</p></li><li><p>If you do these things and make every effort to confirm your calling, you will recieve a rich welcome into heaven. woohoo!</p></li></ul><p>Have self-control.</p>$b$),
  ('2023-11-30', $b$Ezekiel 37:1-39:29$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>We call out to dry bones, come aliveeee come aliivvee ohhh</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$2 Peter 2:1-22$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>False teachers suck</p></li></ul><p>Don't be a false teacher.</p>$b$),
  ('2023-12-01', $b$Ezekiel 40:1-41:26$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Lotta gates.</p></li><li><p>Lotta rooms.</p></li><li><p>A nice temple.</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$2 Peter 3:1-18$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>People will scoff. FU*K THEMMMM</p></li><li><p>Time is different to the LORD. He will keep his promise. Unlike SOME PEOPLEEEEE</p></li><li><p>The day of the LORD will come like a thief. AHHHHH (so always be on your guard)</p></li></ul><p>Time is different to the Lord.</p>$b$),
  ('2023-12-02', $b$Ezekiel 42:1-44:31$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Seems ezekiel got a pretty cool room tour</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$1 John 1:1-10$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>God is light, in him there is no darkness</p></li><li><p>We are not without sin.</p></li></ul><p>Don't walk in the darkness.</p>$b$),
  ('2023-12-03', $b$Ezekiel 45:1-46:24$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>A buncha rules and standards</p></li><li><p>Poor lambs as sacrifice. They didnt do anything. But Jesus didn't either, I guess.</p></li><li><p>Why must the people not come back out through the same gate they came in?</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$1 John 2$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Don't hate your brothers and sisters. That means you'll be walking in darkness.</p></li><li><p>Do not love the world or anything in the world; it will pass away</p></li></ul><p>Do not love the world or anything in it.</p>$b$),
  ('2023-12-04', $b$Ezekiel 47:1-48:35$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>THE ALL BLUE</p></li><li><p>The name of the city is: the lord is there</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$1 John 3$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>God calling us his children is a great love.</p></li><li><p>No one who is born of God continues to sin</p></li><li><p>Love one another as he commanded us</p></li></ul><p>As someone who is born again, don’t continue to sin.</p>$b$),
  ('2023-12-05', $b$Daniel 1:1-2:49$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>“Young men without any physical defect, handsome, showing aptitude for every kind of learning, well informed, quick to understand, and qualified to serve in the king’s palace.” Must be nice.</p></li><li><p>Look at Daniel on that diet. What a top G</p></li><li><p>Good story.</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$1 John 4:1-21$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Do not believe every spirit; test them. Not sure how this applies today, but okay.</p></li><li><p>God is love. Love your brother. Love your sister.</p></li></ul><p>Be disciplined and faithful like Daniel.</p>$b$),
  ('2023-12-06', $b$Daniel 3:1-4:37$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Why is the king so stupid that in the last chapter he fell prostrate before Daniel and the next he wants to throw them in a furnace? What if thats like me… 😳</p></li><li><p>Always thought it was cool that the flames killed the guards too</p></li><li><p>Ai ya, nebuchadnezzar. Rookie mistake.</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$1 John 5:1-21$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Keep yourself from idols.</p></li><li><p>Everyone born of God overcomes the world. Let’s overcome this world.</p></li></ul><p>Keep yourself from idols.</p>$b$),
  ('2023-12-07', $b$Daniel 5:1-7:28$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>What a cold way to kill someone. Giant hand writing on the wall. Would be a sweet domain expansion.</p></li><li><p>At least this new king guy Darius is pretty smart.</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$2 John 1$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Walk in the truth!!!</p></li></ul><p>Try to have some faith like Daniel.</p>$b$),
  ('2023-12-08', $b$Daniel 8:1-10:21$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Goat</p></li><li><p>Daniel used no lotions for three weeks! Wow!</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$3 John 1$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Don't imitate what is evil</p></li></ul><p>Do not imitate what is evil.</p>$b$),
  ('2023-12-09', $b$Daniel 11:1-12:13$b$, null, $b$Jude 1$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Be merciful to those who doubt</p></li><li><p>Save others from the fire</p></li></ul><p>Save others from the fire.</p>$b$),
  ('2023-12-10', $b$Hosea 1:1-4:19$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>“Go marry a promiscuous woman and have children with her” oh, if only God could give me those commands.</p></li><li><p>Imagine being named, “not loved” or “not my people”...</p></li><li><p>Soooo looks like israel is back at it again</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$Revelation 1:1-10$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>God is the alpha and the omega</p></li></ul><p>God has no end or beginning</p>$b$),
  ('2023-12-11', $b$Hosea 5:1-8:14$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Come, let us turn to the lord.</p></li><li><p>As surely as the sun rises, he will appear…i hope so…</p></li><li><p>Idols will be broken in pieces</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$Revelation 2:1-29$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Be faithful, even to the point of death</p></li><li><p>Whoever has ears, let him hear.</p></li></ul><p>TURN TO THE LORD, even when nothing i’m doing seems to be working, all the work i'm doing seems to be going nowhere…turn to the lord, and be faithful, even to death.</p>$b$),
  ('2023-12-12', $b$Hosea 9:1-11:12$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Israel is selling yet again.</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$Revelation 3:1-22$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>“You have a reputation of being alive, but you are dead.” nice.</p></li><li><p>Remember, therefore, what you have learned and hold it fast</p></li><li><p>Don't be lukewarm.</p></li><li><p>He stands at the door and knocks. If anyone were to hear his voice and open the door, he would come in to eat with him. yayyyy</p></li></ul><p>Open my door if I ever hear knocks. Figuratively speaking.</p>$b$),
  ('2023-12-13', $b$Hosea 12:1-14:9$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>God still mad at israel</p></li><li><p>You shall acknowledge no other GooODDDD</p></li><li><p>The ways of the Lord are right, the righteous walk in them, but the rebellious stumble in them.</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$Revelation 4:1-11$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Revelation has some weird creatures.</p></li><li><p>God worthy</p></li></ul><p>Acknowledge no other God</p>$b$),
  ('2023-12-14', $b$Joel 1:1-3:21$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Always kinda wanted to see a locust storm</p></li><li><p>It's never too late to turn to the Lord, even when he’s absolutely shitting on you, for lack of a better term.</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$Revelation 5:1-14$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>I really need a comic version of revelations.</p></li></ul><p>Never too late to turn to the Lord. Don't forget that!</p>$b$),
  ('2023-12-15', $b$Amos 1:1-3:15$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Kinda forgot this book existed</p></li><li><p>Peak poetry</p></li><li><p>Dang, ripping open pregnant women is pretty harsh</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$Revelation 6:1-17$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>What a sight this must've been to see in your dream</p></li><li><p>Who can withstand the wrath of the Lord? ..uh..not me</p></li></ul><p>The power of God is unfathomable. Also I wanna see the horses in revelations.</p>$b$),
  ('2023-12-16', $b$Amos 4:1-6:14$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Seek good, not evil, that you may live</p></li><li><p>The day of the lord will be darkness, not light?</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$Revelation 7:1-17$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>And God will wipe away every tear from their eyes. So nice of God to do that.</p></li></ul><p>Seek good, not evil.</p>$b$),
