  ('2023-12-21', $b$Micah 4:1-5:15$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Everyone will sit under their own vinneee and fig treeeeee</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$Revelation 12:1-17$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>How is a woman clothed in the sun?!?!</p></li><li><p>An oddly created story, I'll say. If it wasn't symbolic, that would be a sight to see.</p></li><li><p>My boy Micheal returns yet again, nice.</p></li><li><p>How does a battle against angels and demons work, I wonder. Guns?</p></li><li><p>The woman has a crown of 12 stars, and the moon at her feet, and the sun as a jacket, but somehow can't fly. And is given eagle wings, like that helps. Which it does.</p></li></ul><p>Everyone will sit under their own vinneee and fig treeee</p>$b$),
  ('2023-12-22', $b$Micah 6:1-7:20$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Shittim</p></li><li><p>Watch in hope for the lord, wait for God your savior</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$Revelation 13:1-18$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>666 astounds me. I don't know if this is one of those things that’s just symbolic or actually holds any meaning.</p></li></ul>$b$),
  ('2023-12-23', $b$Nahum 1:1-3:19$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>The lord is slow to anger but great in power, and he will not leave the guilty unpunished</p></li><li><p>The lord is good, a refuge in times of trouble.</p></li><li><p>Her female slaves moan like doves and beat on their breasts?!?!? okay….</p></li></ul>$b$, $b$Revelation 14:1-20$b$, $b$<ul><li><p>Somehow “harpists playing their harps” sounds kinda odd</p></li><li><p>Also “flying in midair” is like kinda duhhh</p></li><li><p>Wonder how many football fields are in a stadia…</p></li></ul><p>The Lord is a refuge in times of trouble.</p>$b$),
